    {
      "heading": "Third place changes hands",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "person-son-pham-identity-0",
        "person-mark-barney-identity-0",
        "wire-2026-10-15-1159-arc-3-son-mark-ronen-jump-to-third"
      ],
      "text": "Son & Mark & Ronen finishes the reporting day third on the ARC-AGI-3 public board after a five-point improvement to 47.25. The move from seventh puts the team ahead of mtg on 45.00 and NVARC3 on 43.94. Tufa Labs still leads on 68.91, with Yi-Chia Chen second on 67.49: the chase has a new front-runner behind the leading pair, but roughly twenty points still separate third from second. The leaders’ scores are unchanged from the previous close."
    },
    {
      "heading": "The team’s turducken, on the record",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "dispatch-2026-10-15-special-afternoon-argon-and-third-place",
        "person-mark-barney-identity-0",
        "person-son-pham-identity-0"
      ],
      "text": "The afternoon special first reported the gain and an exclusive collective team statement supplied by Mark Barney: “We're using the turducken harness, which is the original duck but it's also inside of a chicken that's inside of a turkey.” The acknowledgment was: “Shoutouts to Tufa, Daniel Franzen, and NVIDIA for open-sourcing their previous work and leading the way.” This is the team’s description, with no further implementation evidence supplied; today’s score does not establish which ingredient caused the gain. The closing roster again lists markbarney, sonphamorg and scizical. Barney is also this paper’s head human editor. Tonight’s commissioned illustration depicts Son and Mark with two cybernetic Yorkies; its nested flying machine and Franzen-avatar duck are editorial metaphor, implying no collaboration or team membership for Franzen."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Argon’s bigger result comes with an unfinished comparison",
      "sourceIds": [
        "social-2110768288523251762",
        "social-2110768292101042240",
        "wire-2026-10-15-1602-arc-3-gemini-argon-verified-results"
      ],
      "text": "Away from Kaggle, ARC Prize announced Gemini 4 Argon at 97.5% on ARC-AGI-3 with a provider adapter, making Google DeepMind the second frontier lab above 95% in its Verified testing. The standard-harness score was 49.8%, but API issues left only 42 of 55 low-reasoning runs complete. Medium reasoning completed 46 games and scored 46.3%; high completed 19, with no published score. Reported scores include all 55 games and preserve partial credit on incomplete runs. The adapter preserves opaque reasoning and allows automatic compaction; the standard harness carries notes between turns. These observations make the evaluation setup consequential, but the incomplete runs prevent treating the headline gap as a clean measure of its effect. Verified model results are separate from this competition’s team standings."
    },
    {
      "heading": "Gold gets harder to hold",
      "sourceIds": [
        "board",
        "wire-2026-10-15-0605-arc-3-two-teams-break-into-gold",
        "wire-2026-10-15-1002-arc-3-gold-line-rises-two-teams-out"
      ],
      "text": "The provisional gold score has risen from 37.18 to 37.98 since the previous close. The entry named speed, my mom is kinda homless sits sixteenth on 38.22, less than a point clear of that score. Its net daily gain is 5.99 points; a wire report’s larger rolling-window gain uses a different starting observation. AquaUrsa Research’s earlier surge was already covered in the Early edition. Tonight’s lesson at the boundary is that a score can hold while its place slips. All public medal positions remain provisional."
    }
  ],
